<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Northern Fury 28 - Bump in the Night, 1994</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Northern Fury&amp;nbsp;28 -&amp;nbsp;Bump in the Night&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = "o" ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;1 March 1994, 2100 Zulu, 2100 Local&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;The new global war – World War Three - has been raging for a couple weeks, NATO has now begun the offensive but the Warsaw Pact is far from defeated as it showed when the Carrier Eisenhower and most of its CVBG were sunk yesterday in a well coordinated and overwhelming attack by submarines and bombers. Resistance on Iceland is stiff but signs of an impending collapse due to isolation are evident. But now the Soviets are threatening offensive operations in Norway.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;The ground war in Europe continues to be brutal and deadly, Berlin has fallen as well as most of the former East Germanybut the Germans continue to govern from the old West German facilities in Bonn. The immediate reinforcement to Europe of the 24&lt;SUP&gt;th&lt;/SUP&gt; Infantry Division (24 ID) and 3&lt;SUP&gt;rd&lt;/SUP&gt; Armored Cavalry Regiment in the first week of the war was quickly followed by III US Corps complete (1 ID, 1 Cav D, 2 AD, 4 ID, 5 ID &amp;amp; Corps Troops) which has largely deployed and is forming in France and Germany but SACEUR is reluctant to commit this force to an offensive yet after the US V and VII counteroffensive ground to a halt around Leipzig earlier this week. A major engagement involving several SSGNs inflicted significant damage on a follow on convoy for the 24&lt;SUP&gt;th&lt;/SUP&gt; ID, much of its ‘round out’ equipment was either sunk or will be delayed. Meanwhile, the 101&lt;SUP&gt;st&lt;/SUP&gt; Air Assault Division has deployed to Egypt to stabilize the situation there and the 82&lt;SUP&gt;nd&lt;/SUP&gt; Airborne Division, which up to now has been the US Strategic Reserve, is deploying to Sicily as the Operational Reserve in Europe. 10&lt;SUP&gt;th&lt;/SUP&gt; Mountain Division is now the Strategic reserve as I Corps has deployed to the Pacific (9&lt;SUP&gt;th&lt;/SUP&gt; Lt Division was enroute to Europe and re-directed to the Philippines when that was threatened, and has now been reinforced by 7&lt;SUP&gt; &lt;/SUP&gt;ID) &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;Aircraft losses in central Europe count in the thousands, troops in the tens of thousands on both sides. Globally, several hundred vessels have been sunk. Conflicts in the Caribbean, Mediterranean, Persian Gulf and Indian Ocean have stabilized, generally in NATO’s favour; both the Panama and Suez Canals remain open and navigable. In the Pacific, 7&lt;SUP&gt;th&lt;/SUP&gt; Fleet has opened a corridor to the Philippines and Taiwan, but was stalled yesterday in an attempt to open a route to Japan.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;South Korea is still under constant air attack and naval blockade, its government collapsed yesterday and there is a degree of political disarray. A convoy is being assembled that will attempt to reach Busan next week with supply, a Brigade and Divisional troops from 25 US ID and an Australian Brigade.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;USS Constellation is retiring to San Diego, what remains of its air group is operating out of Clark Field, Philippines.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN style="mso-ansi-language: EN"&gt;Strike Fleet Atlantic (STRIKFLTLANT), after successfully landing the bulk of 2 MEF (Marine Expeditionary Force) on Iceland, is reeling from the loss of the Eisenhower. The Enterprise CVBG has been rushed out of dry-dock, it was being repaired after sustaining damage in earlier action, and the Nimitz, already heading into the Atlantic will be joined by the HMS Ark Royal.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN style="mso-ansi-language: EN"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN style="mso-ansi-language: EN"&gt;Meanwhile in Norway the Soviets seem to have put their assault on hold.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;With the main Soviet force on the North side of the Trondheimsfjorden, and the Norwegians defending south of that major water feature, the situation is secure enough that the British Commando Bde has been withdrawn in preparation for future operation. The Air Forces in Norway are sparing daily as more and more force is added on both sides. Supplying elements trapped North of the main line is becoming a problem, however, keeping them there is a thorn in the side of the Soviets.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN style="mso-ansi-language: EN"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;This scenario is playable by both sides:&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;It should be fast and furious.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;As NATO you will be charged with resupplying the isolated coastal fort near Orland, it is on the Northern entrance to the &lt;SPAN lang=EN style="mso-ansi-language: EN"&gt;Trondheimsfjorden, and the Soviets need to silence it before their next move.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;However, it is running out of ammunition, food and many other essential stores. There are mines in the area and you will need to install two minefields yourself.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN style="mso-ansi-language: EN"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN style="mso-ansi-language: EN"&gt;As the Soviet player, you are running routine operations to keep NATO under pressure while the next major push is being prepared. You have routine ASuW, ASW, and counter mining operations ongoing, as well as keeping several isolated detachments supplied.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN style="mso-ansi-language: EN"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN style="mso-ansi-language: EN"&gt;It is a clear, cold and – so far – quiet night in Norway.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;---------------------------------------------&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;Designer’s Notes:&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=standard style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=textbody style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;This is the 28&lt;SUP&gt;th&lt;/SUP&gt; scenario of a 58 scenario campaign. See the Northern Fury background document for further insight on the background and happenings so far. The key nuggets&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=textbody style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -18.15pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-FAMILY: Symbol"&gt;· &lt;/SPAN&gt;Cold War continued, no thaw in relations. WP still alive and doing very well. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=textbody style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -18.15pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-FAMILY: Symbol"&gt;· &lt;/SPAN&gt;The 3&lt;SUP&gt;rd&lt;/SUP&gt; World war started 13 Feb. The Warsaw Pact forces led by the Soviet Union attacked NATO and other nations on a global scale. The main blow was in Western Europe but fighting erupted in the Pacific, Caribbean, Middle East and North Africa.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;India has declared a separate war with Pakistan, North Korea attacked Southwards in an apparently independent move and Argentina is threatening the Falklands again (but has not attacked).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=textbody style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=textbody style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;In earlier scenarios to this battle set, you found that the defences in North Norway have collapsed; the Soviet Northern Fleet has put to sea; and Soviet submarines are inflicting damage along the US Eastern seaboard. Iceland fell to the Soviets, and an attempt has been made to interdict the Sea and Air Lines of Communications between North America and Europe. The 2&lt;SUP&gt;nd&lt;/SUP&gt; Fleet (US) and &lt;SPAN lang=EN style="mso-ansi-language: EN"&gt;Strike Fleet Atlantic (2&lt;SUP&gt;nd&lt;/SUP&gt; Fleet + NATO forces) heavily supported by USAF and RAF elements have an amphibious lodgment on Iceland and are planning to clean up that operation and rehabilitate the force before conducting further amphibious operations in central Norway.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=textbody style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -18.15pt"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=textbody style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt 35.85pt; TEXT-INDENT: -18pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-FAMILY: OpenSymbol; mso-fareast-font-family: OpenSymbol; mso-bidi-font-family: OpenSymbol"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-list: Ignore"&gt;•&lt;SPAN style='FONT: 7pt "Times New Roman"'&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;These are tight and congested waters, whichever side you chose, you should check all Naval routes before hitting start.&lt;SPAN style="mso-spacerun: yes"&gt;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;The AI side will have several ships on RTB so to gain more control you should ‘U’ (un-assign) any of your ships from that command and issue your own orders.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=textbody style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt 35.85pt; TEXT-INDENT: -18pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-FAMILY: OpenSymbol; mso-fareast-font-family: OpenSymbol; mso-bidi-font-family: OpenSymbol"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-list: Ignore"&gt;•&lt;SPAN style='FONT: 7pt "Times New Roman"'&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;You have several tasks to complete and limited forces, prioritization is essential.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=textbody style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt 35.85pt; TEXT-INDENT: -18pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-FAMILY: OpenSymbol; mso-fareast-font-family: OpenSymbol; mso-bidi-font-family: OpenSymbol"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="mso-list: Ignore"&gt;•&lt;SPAN style='FONT: 7pt "Times New Roman"'&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;Points are allotted or deducted for losses, achieving special missions and completing objectives. &lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=Textbody0 style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 6pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=Textbody0 style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 6pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt"&gt;Created by Bart Gauvin: AKA Gunner98&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
